// spec: a parenthesised name of a type before a parenthesised value followed by `(`, `.`, `->` or `[` (`(Wide)(twice)(3)`, `(Wide)(box).value`) is an error that asks which is meant: C++ casts the whole postfix expression, `(Wide)((twice)(3))`, the parser reads the cast first; casts one after another, `(Wide)(Word)(3)`, are no such case (language/chained_casts_of_parenthesised_type_names)
// error: parenthesised_type_before_a_postfix_expression_is_error.kpp:19: error: `(T)(x)` followed by `.`, `->`, `[` or `(` is a cast of the whole postfix expression in C++; write `T(x)` or `(T)((x)...)` to say which
// error: parenthesised_type_before_a_postfix_expression_is_error.kpp:20: error: `(T)(x)` followed by `.`, `->`, `[` or `(` is a cast of the whole postfix expression in C++; write `T(x)` or `(T)((x)...)` to say which
using Wide = unsigned long long;

Wide twice(Wide v)
{
  return v * 2;
}

struct Box
{
  Wide value = 4;
};

int main()
{
  Box box;
  Wide a = (Wide)(twice)(3);
  Wide b = (Wide)(box).value;
  std::println(a, " ", b);
  return 0;
}
